<title>MEXICO: Mexico crude port Pajaritos open, Dos Bocas shut.</title>
<headline>Mexico crude port Pajaritos open, Dos Bocas shut.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican crude port Pajaritos in Veracruz state reopened at 0600 local/1200 GMT as weather conditions improved, port officials told Reuters.</p>
<p>Crude port Dos Bocas in Tabasco state remained shut, amid continuing strong winds and high waves.  </p>
<p>Both ports had been closed since Friday as a cold front hit the region.</p>
<p>Dos Bocas ships an average 440,000 barrels per day (bpd) of crude and Pajaritos ships an average 399,000 bpd, according to the latest figures from state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex).</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903)).</p>
